term","subtheme":"Auto OEM cycle - CV replacement & PV premiumization","tag":"Auto-Cycle","theme":"Auto & Mobility","tier":"2"}],"thesis":"Best-ever quarterly top line — **₹184.3cr, +32.3% YoY** — with margin **expanding 63bps to 12.23%** *despite* an unsettled steel pass-through, which is the point: the two big customer settlements (steel, retrospective from ~15 July; conversion cost, retrospective from 1 April for tractors, CV \"very soon\") **land in Q2, not Q1**, so Q1's margin is understated and management says so directly. Underneath, three capacity projects flip from spend to output over the next three quarters — **axle-beam extrusion is live now, the foundry high-pressure mould line doubles capacity in Q3, the axle-shaft facility commissions by September, and the seamless-tube plant does trial production by Q4** — after which forging and casting need no further capex at ~70% utilisation. The soft spot is honesty about the base: Q1's 34% trailer-axle growth against a single-digit industry was **partly Q4FY26 order spillover into a capacity that had been the binding constraint**, and management declined to claim share gains.","trig":[]},"lm":"2026-05","m":1404,"mem":0,"pdd":"","prev_stage":1,"prev_zone_vpe":null,"r":12.9,"s":"KROSS","sig":"","sx":{"SMA_50":"196.3","base_count":"","drawdown_from_prev_signal":"","duration_from_prev_signal":"","pct_below_52w_high":"8.0","pct_change_from_prev_signal":"","pivot_close":"","pivot_low":"","stage_changed_since_prev_signal":"","vpe_df_60d_sum":"-2.6","vpe_zone_cumul_df":""},"t":""}},"s":"KROSS"}